# Ticket pipeline (pointer)

Active **GitHub issue `#N`** and/or **open PR** work follows a **fixed stage order**. Track a **pointer** to the current stage. Advance forward only when that stage passes. **Any code fix rewinds the pointer to `BUGBOT`** (then move forward again).

This mirrors SmartAstro’s Bugbot-cycle pipeline, adapted for Integral (GitHub + Python + Tkinter + spec/ADR gate).

## Hard gate — tickets must close on merge

A ticket is **not done** until **all** of these are true:

1. PR merged into `main`
2. GitHub issue `#N` state is **`CLOSED`**
3. Feature branch gone from `origin` (repo `delete_branch_on_merge` + `--delete-branch`)

**Never** end a merge turn while `gh issue view {N} --json state -q .state` is still `OPEN`.

After every merge the human asked for, run:

```powershell
.\scripts\post_merge_hygiene.ps1 -Issue {N} -PR {PR}
```

Or the inline steps in **Post-merge hygiene** below. Missing `Closes #N` in the PR body is a defect — fix by closing the issue manually in the same turn.

## Stages (in order)

```
IMPLEMENT → BUGBOT → TESTS → ARCHITECT → DEPLOY
```

| Stage | What happens | Advance when |
|-------|----------------|--------------|
| **IMPLEMENT** | Ship code/docs for AC (and approved `docs/specs/` when required), review feedback, or CI fixes | Chunk ready for review → **BUGBOT** |
| **BUGBOT** | `/review-bugbot` · `Diff: branch changes` | **Clean** on current diff → **TESTS** |
| **TESTS** | `tests/test_*.py` (prefer `test_*_{N}.py` or issue refs in names for regressions); `python -m py_compile` on touched modules; `python -m pytest` (targeted, then broader if risky) | **Pass** → **ARCHITECT** |
| **ARCHITECT** | `/review-architect` pre-merge gate (`.cursor/rules/integral-architect.mdc`) | **Merge-ready** → **DEPLOY** |
| **DEPLOY** | Validate, push, PR with `Closes #N` (required), watch checks; on human merge ask: merge with branch delete + **verify issue `#N` is CLOSED** via `scripts/post_merge_hygiene.ps1` | Human **merge/sign-off** + issue closed + branch gone → **exit** |

## Rewind rules (mandatory)

| Situation | Pointer moves to |
|-----------|------------------|
| Bugbot reports findings | Stay **BUGBOT** — fix, re-run Bugbot until clean |
| Tests fail or test fixes change behavior | **BUGBOT** |
| Architect reports blockers | **BUGBOT** — fix, re-run Bugbot → Tests → Architect |
| PR/CI/human review needs code changes | **IMPLEMENT** — then **BUGBOT** before skipping ahead |

**Never skip BUGBOT** after a code change, including “phase 2”, session resume, or post-architect fixes.

## Spec / ADR gate (Integral-specific)

- If the change is a **new user-facing feature** without an approved spec, create/amend `docs/specs/...` first (`status: approved`) per ADR-007 / `.cursor/rules/spec-driven-workflow.mdc` — then **IMPLEMENT**.
- Bug fixes and docs/rules-only work may skip a new spec when no ADR/spec conflict exists.
- Spec AC is the product contract; Bugbot/tests/architect verify it.

## Exit (human sign-off + ticket closed)

1. Human says ticket is **done** / asks to **merge**
2. PR **merged** into `main`
3. Linked GitHub issue `#N` is **CLOSED** (not left open)
4. Feature branch deleted on remote (repo setting + merge flag)
5. Agent reports: issue closed + branch deleted (or hygiene script output)

### Post-merge hygiene (mandatory when human asks to merge)

Run immediately after a successful merge — do **not** treat the ticket as finished while the issue is still open:

```powershell
# One-shot (preferred)
.\scripts\post_merge_hygiene.ps1 -Issue {N} -PR {PR}

# Equivalent manual steps:
gh pr merge {PR} --merge --delete-branch
gh issue view {N} --json state,closedAt
if ((gh issue view {N} --json state -q .state) -ne "CLOSED") {
  gh issue close {N} --reason completed --comment "Closed after PR #{PR} merged to main."
}
git fetch --prune origin
gh issue list --state open --limit 20
```

**PR body requirement:** every ticket PR must include a closing keyword on its own line near the top of the body, e.g.:

```text
Closes #N
```

Do not rely on the title alone. Prefer `Closes` / `Fixes` / `Resolves` (GitHub auto-close keywords).

**Branch delete:** `gh pr merge ... --delete-branch`. Repo setting `delete_branch_on_merge` must stay `true`:

```powershell
gh api repos/earthboundtrev/integral --jq .delete_branch_on_merge
# expect: true
```

If a merge leaves a remote feature branch, delete it: `git push origin --delete {branch}` then `git fetch --prune origin`.

**Duplicates:** before `gh issue create`, search open issues for the same title/topic. If extras were created, close them as duplicates when the canonical issue ships (or immediately if never linked to a PR).

**Local cleanup:** after merge, delete the local feature branch (`git branch -d …`) and prune (`git fetch --prune`). Stale `origin/feature/…` refs are not open tickets — prune them so they do not look “still open.”

## Session resume

1. Sync git + read issue/PR (`gh issue view` / `gh pr view`).
2. If the branch diff changed since last **clean Bugbot**, set pointer to **BUGBOT** (not IMPLEMENT-only).
3. Report: `Pipeline pointer: <STAGE>`.
4. If the PR is already merged but issue `#N` is still OPEN → run post-merge hygiene before any new work on that ticket.

## Standalone `/review-bugbot` or `/review-architect`

No active ticket → report findings only unless the user asks to fix. Ticket work always uses this pipeline.

## Response format (active ticket)

End substantive work with:

**Pipeline:** `IMPLEMENT` | `BUGBOT` | `TESTS` | `ARCHITECT` | `DEPLOY` — plus one line each for Bugbot (clean / N fixed), tests (pass/fail), architect (merge-ready / blockers), deploy/PR/CI state, and **next stage**. After merge: explicitly state issue `#N` CLOSED and branch deleted.
